# Investment Tracker Caddy site config (blue/green ready).
# Install to /etc/caddy/Caddyfile on the server (one-time), then reload Caddy.
#
# The reverse_proxy upstream is kept in a SEPARATE file that the deploy script
# rewrites to point at the active color's port (8081 blue / 8082 green). Caddy's
# graceful `reload` then swaps traffic with zero dropped connections.

investtrack.duckdns.org {
	encode gzip zstd
	import /etc/caddy/investtrack-upstream.caddy
}

# --- One-time setup on the server (see docs Runbook C) --------------------
# 1. Create the initial upstream file at the CURRENT port (8080) so nothing
#    breaks during prep:
#      echo 'reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080' | sudo tee /etc/caddy/investtrack-upstream.caddy
# 2. Install this Caddyfile (back up the old one first):
#      sudo cp /etc/caddy/Caddyfile /etc/caddy/Caddyfile.pre-bluegreen
#      sudo cp Caddyfile.example /etc/caddy/Caddyfile
#      sudo caddy validate --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile && sudo systemctl reload caddy
# 3. Install the switch helper + sudoers (see Runbook C). The next deploy then
#    brings up blue on 8081 and removes the legacy 8080 container.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
